WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:04.809
Jonathan nearly bumped into Marissa on his way to the school cafeteria on Monday.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:12.443
He flashed her a smile, but Marissa's eyes narrowed before she quickly looked away and rushed past him.

3
00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:16.693
Jonathan knew he had to do something about her. And about her father.

4
00:00:16.694 --> 00:00:20.610
He needed to grow a backbone—a very large backbone.

5
00:00:20.611 --> 00:00:28.936
He was so distracted at lunchtime, he dipped his French fries in milk instead of ketchup, and he bit into his orange before remembering to peel it. Later

6
00:00:28.937 --> 00:00:35.357
he got out his history textbook in science class and accidentally went to his English classroom when it was time for math. It

7
00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:38.429
took him forever to do his homework after school. Whenever

8
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:44.000
he looked at his books, all he saw were soccer balls and Marissa's pretty face. During

9
00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:47.126
dinner that night, Jonathan's mother frowned. "You

10
00:00:47.127 --> 00:00:52.184
love meatloaf, but you've hardly touched it tonight. What's the matter, Johnnyboy?" "Please

11
00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:57.499
don't call me that, Mom. I'm not a baby anymore," Jonathan said. "I'll

12
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.641
try not to," Mrs. Cho promised. "But tell me what's wrong." Jonathan

13
00:01:01.642 --> 00:01:04.992
speared his meatloaf with his fork. "I

14
00:01:04.992 --> 00:01:08.512
wish I were on a different soccer team," he muttered. Mr.

15
00:01:08.513 --> 00:01:10.980
Cho nodded his agreement. "I

16
00:01:10.981 --> 00:01:15.909
wish you were too. I don't like how your coach is running things," he said. "I'll

17
00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:20.897
call him tomorrow and tell him to give you and the other boys more chances with the ball." "Good idea,"

18
00:01:20.898 --> 00:01:27.149
Jonathan's mother said. "I'll talk to him too and ask him to stop yelling at the team." Pastrami yapped

19
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:32.392
in support. Or maybe he just wanted food. Jonathan slipped

20
00:01:32.393 --> 00:01:37.819
Pastrami some meatloaf under the table. He thought

21
00:01:37.819 --> 00:01:43.292
about his parents' offers to speak to his coach. That would make things easy for him. But how

22
00:01:43.293 --> 00:01:47.957
could he complain about his parents babying him if he let them speak on his behalf? Jonathan looked

23
00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:52.280
up and shook his head. "Thanks for offering to help. I appreciate

24
00:01:52.281 --> 00:01:56.714
it. But I want to handle things myself." His mother

25
00:01:56.715 --> 00:02:03.196
peered closely at him. "That's fine, Jonathan. But how?" she asked. Jonathan shrugged.

26
00:02:03.197 --> 00:02:09.123
He wasn't exactly sure what he would do. But he had to do something . "Well,

27
00:02:09.124 --> 00:02:14.278
we'll back you up," his dad said. "You can always count on us." "Thanks,"

28
00:02:14.279 --> 00:02:16.607
Jonathan said. Mrs.

29
00:02:16.608 --> 00:02:21.850
Cho grinned. "But only if you stop feeding Pastrami under the table!" Jonathan grinned

30
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:26.849
back. His parents were pretty smart sometimes! * *

31
00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:34.006
* By the next day, Jonathan had a plan. After school he walked to the park across the

32
00:02:34.007 --> 00:02:45.670
street. He found Max there, just as he'd expected, kicking a soccer ball against a wall with his left foot and then his right and then his left, over and

33
00:02:45.671 --> 00:02:48.646
over. Practicing soccer alone seemed really

34
00:02:48.647 --> 00:02:51.499
boring. "Can I talk to you?" Jonathan

35
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:57.488
asked. Max trapped the ball under one foot and turned toward Jonathan. "Sure. What's

36
00:02:57.488 --> 00:03:03.225
up?" "I want to apologize," Jonathan said. "I've been blaming you for things that your dad

37
00:03:03.226 --> 00:03:06.456
does. It's not your fault that he makes everyone give you the

38
00:03:06.457 --> 00:03:11.456
ball." He grinned. "Just like it's not my fault that my mom calls me

39
00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:18.799
Johnnyboy." Max smiled too. "Thank you for that. My dad is very demanding, but at least he doesn't call me a dumb name."

40
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.966
"Whoa!" Jonathan said. He made his eyes bulge out and dropped his jaw as far as it could go.

41
00:03:24.967 --> 00:03:28.648
"Why are you making that crazy face?" Max asked.

42
00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:34.423
"Because I'm in shock from witnessing a miracle: Max Wattenbarger actually smiled."

43
00:03:34.424 --> 00:03:42.191
Max smiled wider. "I should do that more often—it feels good. I know I take soccer too seriously sometimes."

44
00:03:42.192 --> 00:03:51.125
He hesitated for a second. "And I need to apologize to you too. I should have asked my dad to give everyone on the team a chance with the ball.

45
00:03:51.126 --> 00:03:54.433
I didn't want to hurt his feelings or make him mad.

46
00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:58.774
He's so proud of me, and he works really hard to make me a better soccer player.

47
00:03:58.775 --> 00:04:04.258
Plus, honestly, I couldn't get up the nerve to ask him. He'd get furious at me."

48
00:04:04.259 --> 00:04:10.674
"I should have asked him too," Jonathan said. "I didn't have the nerve either. I get it." "Good,

49
00:04:10.675 --> 00:04:18.093
but can you get this?" Max ran off with the ball, dribbling it through the park. Jonathan

50
00:04:18.094 --> 00:04:27.415
chased after him, but Max was too fast. Suddenly Carlos ran over and stole the ball from Max. "Nice

51
00:04:27.416 --> 00:04:31.749
going," Jonathan said. "When did you get here?" "Just

52
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.567
now," Carlos replied. "I

53
00:04:34.568 --> 00:04:40.321
spotted someone dribbling a soccer ball faster than the speed of light, and I knew it had to be Max." "Don't

54
00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:45.060
exaggerate," Jonathan said. "Max doesn't run that fast. Though

55
00:04:45.061 --> 00:04:49.139
he can probably beat most cars, trains, and airplanes." Max

56
00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.464
laughed. Jonathan

57
00:04:52.465 --> 00:05:00.980
pretended to faint. He said, "Max, you set two huge records today. You smiled and you laughed." Soon

58
00:05:00.981 --> 00:05:04.895
all three boys were laughing. Then

59
00:05:04.896 --> 00:05:13.383
they kicked the ball around and practiced the double fake and hip fake moves that Max had taught them the week before. When

60
00:05:13.383 --> 00:05:16.962
they got tired, they sat on the grass. "A few

61
00:05:16.963 --> 00:05:22.209
weeks ago, I only wanted to win soccer games," Carlos said. "But it's

62
00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:28.708
no fun to win soccer if you hardly ever get the ball. I'd rather lose and have fun." "Me too,"

63
00:05:28.709 --> 00:05:31.482
Jonathan agreed. Max nodded

64
00:05:31.483 --> 00:05:33.535
glumly. "My dad

65
00:05:33.535 --> 00:05:38.447
means well, but having me hog the ball isn't fair to the rest of the team." Carlos started

66
00:05:38.448 --> 00:05:45.019
laughing. "At one point Jonathan was so mad at you, he was scheming ways to get rid of you. He wanted

67
00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:49.503
to infect you with cold germs so you'd get too sick to play!" Jonathan instantly

68
00:05:49.504 --> 00:05:54.363
felt bad. "I wasn't serious about that!" Max shrugged.

69
00:05:54.364 --> 00:05:58.931
"It's cool. We're friends now." "How about

70
00:05:58.931 --> 00:06:01.915
a group hug?" Jonathan joked. Carlos pretended

71
00:06:01.916 --> 00:06:04.335
to throw up. "How about

72
00:06:04.335 --> 00:06:07.522
a fist bump instead?" Max asked. Jonathan nodded

73
00:06:07.524 --> 00:06:12.553
and held up his fist. * *

74
00:06:12.553 --> 00:06:18.006
* On the way home later, Jonathan thought about how a lot of people had been changing their minds lately.

75
00:06:18.007 --> 00:06:21.157
His parents had changed their minds about contacting the coach.

76
00:06:21.158 --> 00:06:24.985
Carlos had changed his mind about winning soccer at all costs.

77
00:06:24.986 --> 00:06:30.818
And Jonathan had changed his own mind about Max. Max was actually a pretty nice kid.

78
00:06:30.819 --> 00:06:36.726
"So maybe," Jonathan thought, "it's possible for Marissa to change her mind about me."

79
00:06:36.727 --> 00:06:46.394
He just had to figure out a way to make that happen.

